{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4539","id":4734389338,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGjEMWg","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4539","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4539.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4539.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4539","number":4539,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A29: fuzz bounded LSP and DAP request sequences","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A29-T05.6\nRelated: #1148.\n\n## Behavior\nExtend the framing adapter with bounded byte-selected request sequences against the actual in-memory LanguageServer and DebugAdapter. LSP exercises two fixed documents, edits, queries, diagnostics, close and shutdown. DAP exercises fixed-assembly launch, configuration, bounded execution/stepping/inspection, restart and disposal.\n\nInputs can select only reviewed operations and fixed payloads. Each sequence has at most32 operations; document text, token cache, instructions, emitted messages and cumulative output are bounded. The fixed DAP fixture does not select host paths, arbitrary assemblies, modules or expressions. Callback failures escape the handler error boundary, and owned sessions are disposed.\n\nExpected negative responses require exact intentional product diagnostics. Caught native exceptions remain findings. Null/malformed DAP and LSP parameter cases stay reachable by mutation; regression tests explicitly preserve the known defects instead of declaring them conformance passes.\n\n## Ownership and limits\nThis PR changes only the A29 adapters and tests. The separate minimal LSP container fix is #4536. The DAP null-envelope/null-argument product prerequisite remains with the active A14 owner of packages/protocol/src/dap.js. No general arbitrary-application execution or external VS Code client qualification is claimed.\n\n## Validation\n- 40 focused protocol-sequence and existing text-target tests passed.\n- Command: `node scripts/limited.js node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap tests/conformance/fuzz/protocol-sequences.test.js tests/conformance/fuzz/text-targets.test.js`.\n- Node24.19.0, Linux x64; local tested commit `6ee824fa5af0645cda1125c32661898f681825fb`, tree `2742287d1fd0059469ce859ef521264997b6fa48`.\n- Published tree verified byte-identical; GitHub-created commit metadata differs. Independent source review passed.\n- Test cases remain covered by the existing A29 manifest glob. Ordinary core checks static/build behavior and do not execute Node tests.\n\nThe broader malformed-request and affected-platform acceptance remains open.","created_at":"2026-10-04T12:33:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T12:35:50Z","closed_at":"2026-10-04T12:35:49Z","merged_at":"2026-10-04T12:35:49Z","merge_commit_sha":"e1f1571b34a2abc83f1e49eeda65d8115c6a35ef","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":12525232279,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU